<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Common Program</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1949</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Common Program was the provisional constitution of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peoples-republic-of-china">People's Republic of China</a>, adopted by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chinese-peoples-political-consultative-conference">Chinese People's Political Consultative Conference</a> on 29 September 1949. It defined the new state as a people's democratic dictatorship led by the working class and set out a coalition with other classes and parties. It was replaced by the first constitution of the People's Republic in 1954.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/common-program.jpg" alt="Common Program" width="320" height="337" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Chinese People's Political Consultative Conference · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chinese_People%27s_Political_Consultative_Conference_logo.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
